    "content": "<article> <h3>A typical solution</h3> <p>Here is a function that processes an array:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-cpp\" data-lang=\"cpp\">auto process_values(const std::vector&lt;uint8_t&gt; &amp;vec)\n{\n    return std::count_if(\n        vec.begin(),\n        vec.end(),\n        [](uint8_t x) { return x % 2 == 0; }\n    );\n}</code></pre> <p>Let's look at the generated assembly:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-nasm\" data-lang=\"nasm\">process_values():\n    vpbroadcastb    xmm1, byte ptr [rip + .LCPI0_1]\n    vmovd   xmm2, dword ptr [rsi + rax]\n    vpandn  xmm2, xmm2, xmm1\n    add     rax, 4\n    cmp     r8, rax\n    jne     .LBB0_6</code></pre> <p>The compiler generates vectorized code that processes four values at a time.</p> </article>",
    "contentMarkdown": "### A typical solution\n\nHere is a function that processes an array:\n\n```cpp\nauto process_values(const std::vector<uint8_t> &vec)\n{\n    return std::count_if(\n        vec.begin(),\n        vec.end(),\n         { return x % 2 == 0; }\n    );\n}\n```\n\nLet's look at the generated assembly:\n\n```nasm\nprocess_values():\n    vpbroadcastb    xmm1, byte ptr [rip + .LCPI0_1]\n    vmovd   xmm2, dword ptr [rsi + rax]\n    vpandn  xmm2, xmm2, xmm1\n    add     rax, 4\n    cmp     r8, rax\n    jne     .LBB0_6\n```\n\nThe compiler generates vectorized code that processes four values at a time.",
